      <p class="label">Bottineau Rep · Company</p>
      <h1 class="title mt-4 text-[clamp(3.75rem,7vw+1rem,8.5rem)]">A company that stays together all winter</h1>
      <div class="body-copy mt-8 space-y-4">
        <p>Seven actors started Bottineau Rep in 1998, in a storefront on Central Avenue with forty folding chairs and a curtain on a shower rail. They wanted one thing the big houses couldn't give them: to play a whole season together, part after part, as the old repertory companies did.</p>
        <p>In 2006 the company moved into the Sash Works, a sash-and-door factory of 1912 between the river and the rail yards, and built a 62-foot fly tower into its old boiler house. Today twelve actors play the whole season on a 36-week contract, with guest directors and designers, and every cloth is painted on our own paint frame.</p>
      </div>
